# Frontend Integration Guide

This document reflects the current code in `server/src` exactly as implemented right now. It includes a few route and model quirks that the frontend must know about.

Implementation notes:
- `POST /auth/login` is defined once in `server/src/routes/auth_routes.py`; the auth router is mounted under both `/auth` and `/v1/auth`.
- `UploadedFile` in `server/src/models/file_model.py` does not currently define `user_id` or `folder_id`, even though older migrations and one delete service path reference them.
- FastAPI default error payloads are used; custom error envelopes are not implemented.
- **(2026-08-07)** Startup helper logs were updated to plain text in `server/src/config/redis_server.py`, `server/src/config/database.py`, and `server/src/helpers/get_env.py` for Windows console compatibility.
- **(v3.1)** `auth_router` is now mounted under **both** `/auth` and `/v1/auth` in `main.py`. All auth endpoints are accessible via either prefix (e.g. `POST /auth/login` and `POST /v1/auth/login` resolve to the same handler).
- **(v3.1)** `UploadedFile` model now includes a `source_type` column (`Enum: FTP | GDrive | Sharepoint`, nullable).
- **(v3.1)** Google OAuth scopes now include `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.readonly` in addition to `openid`, `email`, `profile`.
- **(Module 1 Tested 2026-07-30)** `_ensure_utc()` helper added to `auth_services.py`. Expiry comparisons in `verify_otp` and `reset_password` now normalise DB-returned naive datetimes to UTC-aware before comparison. This is a no-op on PostgreSQL but fixes `TypeError` when using SQLite or any tz-naive driver.
- **(Module 1 Tested 2026-07-30)** All 13 auth route handlers confirmed via 51 tests (29 unit + 22 integration) — 100% pass rate. Confirmed behaviors: OTP flow (hardcoded `"123456"` in dev), `HttpOnly` cookie path `/auth` for refresh token, `Authorization` header set on login/verify/refresh responses, `is_verified=False` enforced on unverified login attempts.
- **(Module 2 Tested 2026-07-30)** All 5 dataset route handlers confirmed via 71 tests (46 unit + 25 integration) — 100% pass rate. Confirmed behaviors: case-insensitive duplicate name check; `status` field normalizes (`created`→`Created`, `in progress`→`Draft`); `DELETE /v1/datasets/{id}` performs hard delete (not soft-delete) cascading to all mapping rows; `POST /v1/datasets/{id}/files` enforces strict IDOR — file must be owned by the requesting user via an existing `DatasetFolderFilesMapping`; attaching to a Completed dataset returns 400.
- **(Module 2 Tested 2026-07-30)** `_get_folder_tree()` is idempotent — repeated calls with the same path do not create duplicate `Folder` rows. Path security: absolute paths and `..` traversal segments are rejected with 400.
- **(Module 3 Tested 2026-07-30)** All 5 upload route handlers confirmed via 60 tests (35 unit + 25 integration) — 100% pass rate after one test-defect fix. Confirmed behaviors: `POST /v1/upload/init` returns exactly one of `{created, duplicate_suspected, duplicate_short_circuit}` based on file hash existence and existing mappings; `POST /v1/upload/chunk` uses multipart/form-data with atomic Lua bitmap state (prevents duplicate chunk processing); `POST /v1/upload/finalize` enforces 409 when bitcount < total_chunks; master_hash is verified at both init and finalize; wrong-user sessions return 403; ghost sessions return 404.
- **(Module 3 Tested 2026-07-30)** `pg_insert(...).on_conflict_do_nothing()` in `finalize_upload` is PostgreSQL-specific — successfully patched with a SQLite-compatible wrapper in all tests without changing production code. Full end-to-end upload round-trip (init → chunk → finalize → visible in GET /v1/uploads tree) confirmed working.
- **(v4.0)** FTP Bulk Ingestion added via `ftp_watcher.py` background daemon thread. No new HTTP endpoints — ingestion is triggered automatically by polling `uploads/ftp_dropzone/{username}/` every 10 seconds. Files are moved to `uploads/files/FTP/`, deduplicated via SHA-256 `master_hash`, and linked to an auto-created `"FTP Drops"` dataset per user. The watcher uses `source_type='FTP'` on the `uploaded_files` row.
- **(v3.3 Component 1 Tested 2026-08-10)** External FTP Pull Ingestion Gatekeeper added: `POST /v1/ingest/ftp/connect` and `POST /v1/ingest/ftp/disconnect`. Features: AES-256 Fernet password encryption, Redis credential vault (`ext_ftp:creds:{user_id}`, 1800s idle TTL), sliding-window rate limiting (5 req / 5 min), `ftplib.FTP_TLS` connection probe with `allow_insecure` fallback, and dual-path disconnect (graceful draining vs force nuke with reference-counted physical file cleanup). Confirmed via 39 unit/integration tests (188/188 total suite pass rate).
- **(v3.3 Component 2 Tested 2026-08-10)** External FTP Pull Ingestion Navigator added: `GET /v1/ingest/ftp/tree`. Features: Lazy remote FTP directory exploration via `ftplib.FTP.mlsd`, ISO 8601 UTC timestamp conversion (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`), parent path computation, folder-first sorting, and instant control connection cleanup (`ftp.quit()`). Confirmed via unit & integration tests (199/199 total suite pass rate).
- **(v3.3 Component 3 Tested 2026-08-10)** External FTP Pull Ingestion Dispatcher added: `POST /v1/ingest/ftp/init`. Features: Database columns `bytes_downloaded` and `total_bytes` on `AsyncIngestionJob`, Alembic migration `f979e65675e6`, Two-Tier Semaphores (`HostSemaphore` and `UserSemaphore` via Redis), draining session queue lock (409 Conflict), dataset/folder IDOR validation (404/403), recursive folder item expansion, and `202 Accepted` response returning queued jobs list. Confirmed via 204 unit & integration tests (204/204 total suite pass rate).
- **(v3.3 Component 4 Tested 2026-08-10)** External FTP Pull Ingestion Engine & Medic implemented: `process_ftp_ingestion_job(job_id)`. Features: Streaming background worker (`RETR`), Checkpoint Manifest system (`.manifest.json`) supporting range resume via FTP `REST {offset}` without disk re-reads, Session Heartbeat background thread renewing 1800s idle TTL in Redis every 15s during active downloads, Stall Detection (180s zero-byte timeout), SHA-256 deduplication against `UploadedFile`, physical file movement to `uploads/files/FTP/`, dataset mapping insertion, and dataset status synchronization. Confirmed via 205 unit & integration tests (205/205 total suite pass rate).
